"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2997,"Narrated to us Abu Hashim Ziyad ibn Ayyub, narrated to us Ziyad — meaning ibn Abdullah — narrated to us Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said:
Al-Aswad reported:
A’ishah (RA) said:
“I met the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at Al-Abtaḥ while he was ascending and I was descending, or he was descending and I was ascending.”

---

**CHAPTER:**"
2998,"Narrated to us Bundar, narrated to us Abu Bakr meaning Al-Hanafi, narrated to us Aflah who said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad narrate from 'Aishah (RA) who said:

We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and she mentioned the lengthy hadith, saying in the narration: ""Then he (ﷺ) gave permission for departure to his companions from Al-Muhassab. So the people set out, and he (ﷺ) passed by the House before the dawn prayer, performed Tawaf around it, then left. He mounted his ride, then departed heading towards Al-Madinah.""

**CHAPTER:**"
